PUBLIC RESPONSE: {A. Clockwise direction, origin near ton

The phrasing indicates azi (proximal marker) enters and is expressed well before any distal markers, implying an integration site near azi/ton with azi transferred first. The standard E. coli order is thr-leu-azi-ton-pro-lac-gal-str; therefore an Hfr origin near ton that sends azi into the recipient ahead of the remaining chromosome satisfies the data only when transfer proceeds clockwise. All other listed origins/directions place azi either late or among a contiguous early cluster, contradicting the observed long delay before other markers appear.}

}

